      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the experience of Windows environment, ZENKAKU_HANKAKU and EISU in a Japanese BT/USB keyboard are sent as GRAVE and CAPS_LOCK respectively. KEYCODE_ZENKAKU_HANKAKU and KEYCODE_EISU are added as the synonyms of KEYCODE_GRAVE and KEYCODE_CAPS_LOCK.\n\nThey can be discussable but for the case of EISU it\u0027s special. EISU and CAPS_LOCK are exact the same physical key but with different behaviors in Japanese keyboard controlling CAPS_LOCK LED light. In Japanese keyboard user has to press SHIFT+EISU to toggle CAPS_LOCK LED light. In Android it\u0027s not doable by IME above Framework. Underlying Android input module has to distinguish if it\u0027s a EISU or CAPS_LOCK to accomplish different behavior. This is done by feeding Android different .kl files (with different keycodes to the same physical Caps Lock key).",
      "parentUuid": "AAAEGn////A\u003d",
      "revId": "047c38243431e8cb67259635def3e939afa294b9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
